## Verification Strategy

- Unit and API contract tests cover allowlists, validation, identity, enrollment, authorization,
  revocation, idempotency, epochs, unknown semantics, retention, and query projections.
- Reporter tests cover durable outbox recovery, locking, polling, heartbeat, quiescence, retry,
  safety convergence, and portable scheduler command generation.
- Browser and static-site tests cover stable routes, access control, keyboard/focus behavior,
  responsive navigation, and public presentation compatibility.
- PostgreSQL migration, backup/restore, application rollback, load, installed-client canary,
  production health, exact-SHA CI, release, and Hybrid outcome reconciliation close Work5.

## Constraints and Deferrals

- No remote work control, diagnostics invocation, mitigation, automatic repair, or raw-log upload.
- No new identity provider, custom cryptography, Redis, Celery, Kubernetes, broker, HA database,
  replica, multi-region topology, full SPA, SSE, or heartbeat history.
- Existing Rookaro router ownership remains external; this repository changes only its known
  `ts.rookaro.com` deployment target and documents any required route contract.

